+# Triage Labels
+
+Five canonical triage roles used by the `triage` skill. Each role maps to a GitHub label string.
+
+| Role | Label | Meaning |
+|------|-------|---------|
+| needs-triage | `needs-triage` | Maintainer needs to evaluate |
+| needs-info | `needs-info` | Waiting on reporter for more detail |
+| ready-for-agent | `ready-for-agent` | Fully specified, AFK-ready |
+| ready-for-human | `ready-for-human` | Needs human implementation |
+| wontfix | `wontfix` | Will not be actioned |
+
+## Usage
+
+Apply labels via `gh` CLI:
+
+```bash
+gh issue edit <number> --add-label "needs-triage"
+gh issue edit <number> --remove-label "needs-triage" --add-label "ready-for-agent"
+```
+
+## Notes
+
+- An issue starts with `needs-triage` by default when created via `to-issues`.
+- `ready-for-agent` is the terminal triage state before an agent picks it up.
+- `wontfix` is terminal — no further triage occurs.
